+# Fabric backend verification
+
+Verified locally on 2026-10-28 with Minecraft 26.3, Java 25.0.3,
+Fabric Loader 0.19.5, Fabric API 0.162.0+26.3, and Polymer 0.18.5+26.3.
+
+* `:fabric:build` passed, including Java compilation, access-widener validation,
+  and compilation of the separate protocol probe. Existing Javadoc/deprecation
+  warnings remain.
+* A fresh dedicated server reached `Done`, accepted both test clients
+  simultaneously, and shut down cleanly through RCON.
+* The final mixed-client probe passed all **16 assertions**.
+* The vanilla process decoded **3,647 packets** using Mojang's vanilla registries
+  and codecs. It sent no backend opt-in and received no Effortless Building
+  feature/synchronization payloads or custom registry entries.
+* The companion protocol process decoded **1,813 packets**, received backend,
+  config and modifier synchronization, and exercised the real server handlers.
+* The distributable contains Polymer Core/Common and Core's nested
+  networking/registry-sync libraries. Probe classes are excluded from the JAR.
+
+| Area | Verified behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| Opt-in | Build requests before negotiation are ignored, including after a previous connection by the same account. |
+| Building | Server generates and places a three-block line; breaking removes it. |
+| History | Undo removes the line; redo restores it. |
+| Modifiers | An array creates the original block and two offset copies. |
+| Permissions | Spectator placement is rejected. |
+| Materials | Survival placement with two blocks builds only two of three requested positions. |
+| Randomizer | The modded connection receives the real item, opens its custom menu, saves a ratio change, and places the selected material. |
+| Crafting | Identical filled crafting grids produce the tool for the modded player and an empty result for the vanilla player. |
+| Item isolation | Vanilla cannot pick up a dropped tool or shift-click a hidden tool from a shared chest. The tool remains in the chest. |
+| Vanilla gameplay | The vanilla player opens ordinary chests/crafting tables and transfers an ordinary stone item into its hotbar. |
+| Broadcasts | An operator updates server configuration while the vanilla client remains connected without receiving the custom synchronization. |
+
+The local run logs are preserved under
+`fabric/build/reports/backend-compatibility/`: `build.log`, `server.log`,
+`probe.log`, and `stop.log`. The tested JAR is
+`fabric/build/libs/effortlessbuilding-fabric-26.3-4.3.jar`.
+
+These are real network integration tests with headless clients, not a graphical
+Minecraft client play-through. UI rendering/input, AE2, third-party claims,
+and other server platforms were not tested. See the
+[backend guide](fabric-server-backend.md) for reproduction and limitations.
